  "summary": "Power steering (N40) pump mounting on the 454 big-block engine: a bracket bolts to the front of the engine with two bolts, and the pump hangs on it by its own studs (no separate studs) with plain washers, lock washers and nuts, the rear stud going through a slotted brace for belt adjustment. The pump pulley is held by a nut, and two belts (2nd and 3rd tracks) drive it.",
